    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">15 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip ok\">Easy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Linked list</span><span class=\"chip accent\">In-place reversal</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/reverse-linked-list/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 206</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Reverse Linked List</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Walk the list once and turn every arrow around. Three pointers do it: <code>prev</code> (the reversed part), <code>cur</code> (the next node to flip) and <code>nxt</code> (saved before the flip, so the rest of the list is not lost). O(n) time, O(1) space; the recursive form costs O(n) stack.</p>\n"
